  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I am fairly certain this is a client regression. This update has broken my primary world completely, and I could not find any workarounds to this problem.\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Create a new SDK3 world project with a platform and a cube with its box collider to be a trigger\n2. Add an Udon script to the trigger cube and create OnTriggerEnter/Stay/Exit Events that call Debug.Log to print messages\n3. Test world and walk into cube\nExpected behavior: Player entering/staying/exiting cube should trigger the Events in the Udon script above\nActual behavior: These events now fail to fire when any player enters the cube\nNote that trigger events for non-player objects still seem to work, e.g. if a rigidbody pickup is added to the above world and moved into the trigger cube by the player, the pickup will correctly trigger the Events.\nModifying the collision matrix does not appear to be the culprit, as while I added a layer to only collide with PlayerLocal in my actual world that broke, if the layer is left as default as in the example project above, the behavior is still broken.",
